## Summary
Cosmetic/UI changes to the Battleship game. 30/30 tests pass, `tsc --noEmit` clean, build clean.

Per-ship segment data was added to state (with approval) so the fleet panel can be correct — see Feature 2.

### 1. Colors & text (`Cell.tsx`, `Game.tsx`)
- Cell backgrounds: `empty → bg-blue-900`, `ship → bg-gray-400`, `hit → bg-red-500`, `miss → bg-blue-300`
- Title → `BATTLESHIP — Human vs AI`, subtitle `Sink all 5 enemy ships to win.`, page bg → `bg-gray-950`, New Game button → `bg-emerald-600 hover:bg-emerald-700`

### 2. Fleet status panels (`Game.tsx` + `types.ts` + `game.ts`)
Correct ship-level Sunk/Afloat status required per-ship cells, which weren't in state (only the merged 17-cell set). Added (approved):
```ts
// types.ts: GameState gains
playerFleet: number[][];
aiFleet: number[][];
// game.ts: new placeFleet() returns [[...5],[...4],[...3],[...3],[...2]]
// initializeGame() derives playerShips/aiShips = new Set(fleet.flat())
```
`placeAllShips` and all 30 tests are untouched. A ship is **Sunk** (red) when every cell in its segment is in the opposing attacks set, else **Afloat** (green).

### 3. Hit/miss animations (`Cell.tsx`, `index.css`)
Pure-CSS keyframes (no JS libs). `cell-hit` pulses `scale(1) → 1.3 → 1` over 300ms; `cell-miss` fades `opacity 0 → 1` over 200ms.

### 4. Shot counter & accuracy (`Game.tsx`)
```ts
const shots = game.playerAttacks.size;
const hits = [...game.playerAttacks].filter(i => game.aiShips.has(i)).length;
const accuracy = shots === 0 ? '0' : ((hits / shots) * 100).toFixed(1);
// "Shots: X | Hits: Y | Accuracy: Z%"
```

### 5. Layout: side fleet panels + color legend (`Game.tsx`)
- Fleet status moved out of the top into narrow `w-36` side cards in a 3-column `flex flex-row items-start gap-6` layout: `[Your Fleet] [Boards] [Enemy Fleet]`. Each card lists the 5 ships vertically with Afloat/Sunk.
- Color legend (`Empty`/`Your Ship`/`Hit`/`Miss` swatches, `text-slate-400 text-xs gap-4`) added below the boards; New Game button moved below the legend.

