Removes `react-router` entirely (both the CDN script and the npm dependency) in favor of minimal native hash-based routing.

## Changes

- **`script.jsx`**
  - Added `getHashParams()` to parse `window.location.hash` into `{ scriptId, action }`
  - Dropped `ReactRouter.State` mixin from `Script`, `Line`, and `Nav`; replaced all `this.getParams()` calls with `getHashParams()`
  - Replaced `<Link to="/demo">` with `<a href="#/demo">`
  - Replaced `ReactRouter.run()` + `Route`/`DefaultRoute`/`RouteHandler` bootstrap with a simple `App` component rendered on `hashchange`

  ```js
  function getHashParams() {
    var hash = window.location.hash.replace(/^#\/?/, '');
    var parts = hash ? hash.split('/') : [];
    return { scriptId: parts[0] || null, action: parts[1] || null };
  }

  window.addEventListener('hashchange', renderApp);
  renderApp();
  ```

- **`index.html`** — removed `react-router@0.11.6` CDN `<script>` tag
- **`package.json`** — removed `"react-router": "^7.13.0"` from dependencies

New script creation failed with "Cannot read properties of null (reading 'title')" and "Firebase.update failed: First argument contains undefined in property 'firstLine'". The script object was initialized as empty `{}`, then partially updated, leaving required fields undefined.

## Changes

**Firebase initialization (script.jsx:92-97)**
- Create first line before initializing script object
- Use atomic `set()` instead of `set({})` + `update()` sequence
- Initialize with all required fields: `title: ''`, `firstLine: newLine.key`

```javascript
// Before: empty object then update
fb.set({});
var newLine = fb.child('lines').push({ type: 'scene' });
fb.update({ firstLine: newLine.key });

// After: atomic initialization with all fields
var newLine = fb.child('lines').push({ type: 'scene' });
fb.set({
  title: '',
  firstLine: newLine.key
});
```

**Title handling (app.js:94,97 & script.jsx:491-492)**
- Add fallback `|| 'Untitled'` when reading `script.title` for document.title
- Prevents null reference errors during initialization window

